#script to scan 3-inch PMTs as it is done at ECAP by O. Kalekin

#See O. Kalekin presentation at KM3NeT Collaboration Meeting (LNS Jun 2013)
#See 1st KM3NeT-phase1 Collaboration meeting (Marseille Jan 2013)
#See Google Drive-> DET-> PMT -> KM3NeT_PMT_2013_002-Evaluation Report Hamamatsu_R12199.pdf
#QE: monochromator
#DE: 470nm fast LED, optical fiber, XY-scanner
#Effective diameter ~76mm

#Private communication with O. Kalekin:
#It was 1 mm diameter optical fiber with ~3 mm black tube at the output to make the beam more collimated.
#At PMT center, where the distance between optical fiber and PMT was < 1 mm, the diameter of light spot was 1 mm.
#It should increase to the edge, due to spherical shape of PMT.
#Distance from fiber to photocathode at the edge is ~25 mm.
#The size of the light spot at this distance can be estimated from the plot you attached due to some sensitivity beyond physical diameter of PMT.
#My quick estimation: ~5 mm diameter.

#From these data you can make the beam model.
#It was only 1 measurement. Flat parametrization with 76 mm diameter should be enough.

/KM3/XP/Type AA
/KM3/det/DetectorTypeName KM3PMTnaked

/KM3/det/setTargetMaterial IdealWater
/KM3/det/setTargetLength 10 m
/KM3/det/DontDraw bento
#/KM3/det/setOpticalModuleAngle 0.5 deg
/KM3/det/setOpticalModuleTheta 0 deg
/KM3/det/setOpticalModulePhi 0 deg

/KM3/det/setMeanCapRadius 0 cm
/KM3/GenType 1

/run/verbose 0
/run/initialize
/tracking/storeTrajectory 0

/gps/verbose 0
/gps/number 1
/gps/particle opticalphoton
/gps/pos/centre  0 0 400 mm

/gps/pos/type Beam
/gps/pos/shape Circle
/gps/pos/rot1 0 1 0
/gps/pos/rot2 1 0 0

/gps/direction 0. 0. -1.
/gps/pos/radius 1 nm

/gps/ene/type Gauss
#LED 470 nm
/gps/ene/mono  2.637961 eV

/tracking/verbose 0
/event/verbose 0


/vis/open HepRepXML
/vis/scene/create filename.bheprep.zip
/vis/drawVolume
/vis/scene/endOfEventAction accumulate 500
/tracking/storeTrajectory 1

/tracking/verbose 0
/event/verbose 0
/run/beamOn 1000
